#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:0
msgid ""
"Access the snapd REST API through its UNIX socket, authenticate requests, "
"handle JSON responses and errors, and use client libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:8
msgid "Use the REST API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:10
msgid ""
"The REST API provides access to snapd's state and many of its key functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:12
msgid ""
"See below for details on accessing the API,  authentication, JSON elements "
"and error types, and see the {ref}`API reference <reference-development-"
"snapd-rest-api>` for which actions can be performed and which elements can "
"be requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:14
msgid "Accessing the API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:16
msgid ""
"The `/run/snapd.socket` UNIX socket is used to connect a client to the API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:18
msgid ""
"To send a **POST** request with _curl_, for example, the following will ask "
"snapd to install the [hello](https://snapcraft.io/hello) snap from the "
"_edge_ channel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:20
msgid ""
"sudo curl -sS --unix-socket /run/snapd.socket \\\n"
"http://localhost/v2/snaps/hello \\\n"
"-X POST -d '{\"action\": \"install\", \"channel\": \"edge\"}'\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:26
msgid ""
"Similarly, the following curl command will remove a {ref}`quota group <how-"
"to-guides-manage-snaps-use-resource-quotas>` called _allquotas_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:28
msgid ""
"sudo curl -sS --unix-socket /run/snapd.socket \\\n"
"http://localhost/v2/quotas \\\n"
"-X POST -d '{\"action\": \"remove\", \"group-name\": \"allquotas\"}'\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:34
msgid ""
"A request will return a JSON-formatted object. The following example uses "
"_curl_ to **GET** request the list of installed snaps, piped through _jq_ "
"for formatting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:36
msgid ""
"$ sudo curl -sS --unix-socket /run/snapd.socket http://localhost/v2/apps \\\n"
"| jq\n"
"{\n"
"  \"type\": \"sync\",\n"
"  \"status-code\": 200,\n"
"  \"status\": \"OK\",\n"
"  \"result\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"snap\": \"anbox-installer\",\n"
"      \"name\": \"anbox-installer\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:53
msgid ""
"HTTPS connections over a TCP socket are under consideration for a future "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:56
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:58
msgid "The API incorporates three levels of access:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:59
msgid "**open**: API requests will succeed without authorisation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:60
msgid ""
"**authenticated**: requires suitable authorisation to be provided with each "
"request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:61
msgid ""
"**root**: root user gains authenticated access without sending authorisation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:63
msgid ""
"If an app or client is already running as root, it _does not_ require the "
"use of macaroons or any further authentication. The API will by default "
"allow access to anything that needs to be authenticated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:65
msgid ""
"Authorisation is provided by sending a Macaroon with the HTTP authorisation "
"header. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:67
msgid ""
"Authorization: Macaroon root=\"serialized-store-"
"macaroon\",discharge=\"discharge-for-macaroon-authentication\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:71
msgid ""
"If available, [Polkit](https://polkit.pages.freedesktop.org/polkit/) can "
"also be used for authentication. The client may choose to allow user "
"interaction for authentication, e.g. showing a graphical dialogue. This is "
"done by setting an HTTP header (defaults to false):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:73
msgid "X-Allow-Interaction: true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:77
msgid "Responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:79
msgid "For each request, the following JSON object is returned:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:81
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:111
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:133
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:153
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:83
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"type\": \"sync\",\n"
"    \"status-code\": 200,\n"
"    \"status\": \"OK\",\n"
"    \"maintenance\": {\n"
"        \"kind\": \"system-restart\",\n"
"        \"message\": \"system is restarting\"\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:95
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:121
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:143
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:167
msgid "Fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:97
msgid "`type`: One of `sync`, `async` or `error`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:98
msgid "`status-code`: HTTP status code matching the HTTP status line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:99
msgid "`status`: HTTP reason phrase matching the HTTP status line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:100
msgid ""
"`maintenance`: JSON object containing maintenance information (_optional_)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:102
msgid "Maintenance Fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:104
msgid ""
"`kind`: Kind of maintenance restart, one of `system-restart` or `daemon-"
"restart`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:105
msgid "`message`: Text to show to user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:107
msgid "Synchronous response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:109
msgid ""
"For a standard synchronous operation, the following JSON object is returned:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:112
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"type\": \"sync\",\n"
"    \"status-code\": 200,\n"
"    \"status\": \"OK\",\n"
"    \"result\": { \"name\": \"value\" }，\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:123
msgid ""
"In addition to the standard response fields, the following can also be "
"present:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:125
msgid ""
"`result`: Result from the request. This can be any JSON structure and is "
"commonly either an object or an array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:127
msgid "Asynchronous Response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:129
msgid ""
"When a request takes time to complete, an asynchronous response is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:131
msgid ""
"The request is assigned a change id, which can be checked by requesting "
"`GET /v2/changes/[id]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:134
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"type\": \"async\",\n"
"    \"status-code\": 202,\n"
"    \"status\": \"Accepted\",\n"
"    \"change\": \"401\",\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:145
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:169
msgid ""
"In addition to the standard response fields the following can be present:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:147
msgid "`change`: identifier for the change in progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:149
msgid "Error response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:151
msgid "If a request cannot be completed, an error response is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:155
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \"type\": \"error\",\n"
"    \"status-code\": 401,\n"
"    \"status\": \"Unauthorized\",\n"
"    \"result\": {\n"
"        \"message\": \"access denied\",\n"
"        \"kind\": \"login-required\",\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:171
msgid "`result`: Error information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:173
msgid "Result Fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:175
msgid "`message`: Description of the error, suitable for displaying to a user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:176
msgid ""
"`kind`: Unique code for the error, to enable a snapd client to display "
"appropriate behaviour (_optional_)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:177
msgid ""
"`value`: extra information on the error, typically a string for the snap "
"name or an object with fields dependent on the kind (_optional_)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:179
msgid "Client libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:181
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:183
msgid ""
"The [snap-http](https://github.com/canonical/snap-http) package provides a "
"Python interface to the snapd REST API:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:185
msgid "pip install snap-http\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-rest-api.md:189
msgid ""
"See the [snap-http repository](https://github.com/canonical/snap-http) for "
"documentation and usage examples."
msgstr ""
